ems-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[4,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#orange\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Orange, Red & Ginger Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[5,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#gray\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Gray, Blue & Silver Names\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"li\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[\"$L23\",\"$L24\"]}],\"$L25\"]}]]}],\"$L26\",\"$L27\",\"$L28\",\"$L29\",\"$L2a\",\"$L2b\",\"$L2c\",\"$L2d\",\"$L2e\",\"$L2f\"]}],\"$L30\",\"$L31\",\"$L32\",\"$L33\",\"$L34\",\"$L35\"]}]\n23:[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[6,\".\"]}]\n24:[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#multi\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Multi-Color & Pattern Names\"}]\n25:[\"$\",\"li\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"flex items-start gap-2\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"span\",null,{\"className\":\"text-primary font-bold mt-0.5 min-w-[1.5em]\",\"children\":[7,\".\"]}],[\"$\",\"a\",null,{\"href\":\"#faq\",\"className\":\"text-gray-700 hover:text-primary hover:underline transition-colors text-sm leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"FAQ\"}]]}]\n26:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🎨 Why Color-Based Naming Works\"]}]\n27:[\"$\",\"p\",\"3\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Color-based pet naming is one of the oldest and most intuitive traditions in the world. Long before pets had trendy human names or pop culture references, they had descriptive names based on what they looked like. A black cat was simply Shadow or Midnight. A white dog was Snow or Cotton. This tradition persists for a simple reason: it works. Color-based names are intuitive, descriptive, and instantly communicate something real and observable about your pet to everyone who meets them.\"]}]\n28:[\"$\",\"p\",\"4\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"The beauty of color-based naming lies in its infinite variety. There are dozens of words for every shade, from the obvious to the poetic. A brown dog could be Brownie, Cocoa, Mocha, Chestnut, Acorn, or Timber — each evoking a slightly different shade and feeling. This richness of vocabulary means you can find a color name that feels personal and specific rather than generic. Your pet's exact shade of fur, scales, or feathers is unique — the right color name celebrates that uniqueness.\"]}]\n29:[\"$\",\"p\",\"5\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Color names also tend to age well across your pet's lifetime. While a puppy's coat may darken or lighten slightly with age, the fundamental coloring remains a defining characteristic. A name based on your pet's appearance will always feel connected to the actual animal in front of you, creating a lasting sense of fit that purely abstract names sometimes lack.\"]}]\n2a:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"6\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🤍 White & Cream Coat Names\"]}]\n2b:[\"$\",\"p\",\"7\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"White pets have an ethereal, almost magical quality that invites poetic naming. Whether your companion is a Samoyed, Persian cat, albino ferret, or white rabbit, names that evoke snow, winter, and light create an immediate sense of their visual impact. Snow and Snowball are classics for good reason — simple, descriptive, and universally understood. Pearl suggests luminous, precious beauty. Ghost captures white pets' ability to disappear against light backgrounds in a way that's both practical and poetic.\"]}]\n2c:[\"$\",\"p\",\"8\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"For more creative white pet names, consider winter concepts: Blizzard, Avalanche, Frost, and Aspen carry the crisp beauty of cold landscapes. Food names work wonderfully: Coconut, Marshmallow, Vanilla, Tofu, and Mochi all describe that soft, white, sweet quality. Celestial names like Luna, Moon, Star, and Cloud connect white pets to the luminous beauty of the night sky. For breed-specific white pet names, explore our dedicated animal name generators with 160-plus options per species.\"]}]\n2d:[\"$\",\"h2\",\"9\",{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mt-10 mb-4 text-gray-900\",\"children\":[\"🔗 Explore More Color Names\"]}]\n2e:[\"$\",\"p\",\"10\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Explore our name generators for \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"32\",{\"href\":\"/animal/african-grey-parrot/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"African Grey Parrot\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"55\",{\"href\":\"/animal/amur-leopard/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Amur Leopard\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"71\",{\"href\":\"/animal/african-wild-dog/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"African Wild Dog\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"91\",{\"href\":\"/animal/alpine-salamander/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"Alpine Salamander\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\", and \",[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"116\",{\"href\":\"/animal/african-slender-snouted-crocodile/\",\"className\":\"text-primary font-semibold hover:underline\",\"children\":[\"African Slender-Snouted Crocodile\",\" Name Generator\"]}],\" to find the perfect name for your companion.\"]}]\n2f:[\"$\",\"p\",\"11\",{\"className\":\"text-gray-700 leading-relaxed mb-4\",\"children\":[\"Browse our complete collection: white dog names, black cat names, orange tabby names, and hundreds more. Each animal page features names organized by category including color-themed collections. Visit our animal facts pages for fascinating information about coat color genetics and breed standards.\"]}]\n30:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12 bg-white rounded-2xl p-6 border border-gray-100\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"❓ Frequently Asked Questions\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"space-y-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"details\",\"0\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What if my pet's coat color changes as they age?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Many pets, especially puppies and kittens, experience coat color changes as they mature. If you are naming a young pet based on color, observe the coat closely and research breed-typical color development. A name like Shadow works for most dark coats regardless of exact shade, while very specific color names like Copper might not fit as well if the coat shifts significantly.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"1\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Are color names too obvious or boring?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Color names are only boring if you choose the most obvious option. Snow is a perfectly fine name, but Albedo — the scientific term for reflectivity — is genuinely unique. Shadow is classic, but Penumbra — the partial shadow during an eclipse — is unforgettable. The key is finding the specific shade of language that matches the specific shade of your pet.\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"details\",\"2\",{\"className\":\"bg-gray-50 rounded-xl p-5 group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"summary\",null,{\"className\":\"font-semibold cursor-pointer group-open:text-primary\",\"children\":\"What about multi-colored or patterned pets?\"}],[\"$\",\"p\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-3 text-gray-600 leading-relaxed\",\"children\":\"Multi-colored pets offer the richest creative opportunities. A black and white pet could be Oreo, Domino, Panda, Tuxedo, or Yin Yang. A calico or tortoiseshell cat might be Patch, Mosaic, Kaleidoscope, or Picasso. Brindle coats suggest names like Stripe, Tiger, or Marble. Patterns are unique identifiers — let them inspire equally unique names.\"}]]}]]}]]}]\n31:[\"$\",\"section\",null,{\"className\":\"mt-12\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"h2\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl font-bold mb-6\",\"children\":\"🐾 Related Animal Name Generators\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-3 md:grid-cols-4 gap-3\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"blue-morpho-butterfly\",{\"href\":\"/animal/blue-morpho-butterfly/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🦋\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700 group-hover:text-primary\",\"children\":\"Blue Morpho Butterfly\"}]]}],[\"$\",\"$L3\",\"giant-african-millipede\",{\"href\":\"/animal/giant-african-millipede/\",\"className\":\"bg-white rounded-xl p-4 text-center border border-gray-100 shadow-sm hover:shadow-md hover:border-primary/30 transition-all group\",\"children\":[[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-2xl mb-1\",\"children\":\"🪱\"}],[\"$\",\"div\",null,{\"className\":\"text-sm font-semibold text-gray-700